snapshot-wiki (0.1.3) unstable; urgency=low

  * Remove the Autopsy page (docs/tools/forensics/autopsy.md). The wiki
    documents what the image carries; Autopsy is not on it, and The Sleuth
    Kit is the disk and image examination tool the wiki names.
  * The Sleuth Kit, TestDisk/PhotoRec, field kit, evidence handling,
    lessons-learned, architectures and vendor layer pages no longer mention
    Autopsy. Evidence handling and the field kit hand-off point at The
    Sleuth Kit; the hand-off to an analysis workstation stays, without
    naming a tool for the workstation. Lessons learned takes disk timelines
    from fls -m and mactime.

 -- Blackbird Cyber <snapshot@example.invalid>  Wed, 07 Oct 2026 12:45:00 -0400

snapshot-wiki (0.1.2) unstable; urgency=low

  * Autopsy page rewritten as not shipped (status: not-shipped, no
    launcher): the vendor layer disabled Autopsy on 2026-10-07 because it
    is Windows-first, its Linux build is a documented subset, and fitting
    it into an offline, read-only, quiet-on-the-wire image kept exposing
    new assumptions. It points at The Sleuth Kit, TestDisk/PhotoRec, the
    field kit and the analysis-workstation hand-off instead.
  * Field kit page: "Hand-off to an analysis workstation" (Autopsy's
    Windows build, installed by the operator; the case folder with
    SHA256SUMS and a relative-path transfer manifest as the transfer
    unit). Evidence handling and the IR triage playbook link to it.
  * The Sleuth Kit, TestDisk/PhotoRec, architectures, vendor layer,
    desktop, live and install, wire classes, the ATT&CK for ICS overview
    and the preparation, eradication and lessons-learned phases no longer
    say Autopsy ships, nor that it needs 8 GB of RAM.
  * hooks/snapshot_wiki.py: the facts box of a not-shipped tool without a
    launcher says "none" and "no menu launcher" instead of "run it from a
    terminal" and "its launcher stays hidden".

 -- Blackbird Cyber <snapshot@example.invalid>  Wed, 07 Oct 2026 12:30:00 -0400

snapshot-wiki (0.1.1) unstable; urgency=low

  * pymodbus page: the console launcher is gone (pymodbus-repl dropped from
    the vendor layer) and the serial client works (pyserial vendored), so
    the known-issues admonition goes and the Modbus RTU example returns.
  * /etc/xdg/mimeapps.list: open text/plain in org.xfce.mousepad.desktop.
    With no default, exo-open opened the Field Kit guide
    (fieldkit-guide.txt) in LibreOffice Writer.

